Subject: batman-adv: set the priority of forwarded multicast packets

batadv_skb_set_priority() gives a packet the priority of its payload
(VLAN PCP or IP DSCP) where a node sends it, forwards it as unicast and
rebroadcasts it, so that a relay queues it as the sender did. The path
that forwards the multicast packet type does not call it, and relays send
those packets at priority 0: voice and other marked multicast lose their
priority at the first hop.

Set it in batadv_recv_mcast_packet() before the tracker TVLV is processed,
which makes the forwarded copies.

---
--- a/net/batman-adv/routing.c
+++ b/net/batman-adv/routing.c
@@ -1426,6 +1426,11 @@
 	if (tvlv_buff_len & 1)
 		goto free_skb;
 
+	/* forwarded copies keep the priority of the payload, as unicast and
+	 * broadcast packets do
+	 */
+	batadv_skb_set_priority(skb, hdr_size + tvlv_buff_len);
+
 	ret = batadv_tvlv_containers_process(bat_priv, BATADV_MCAST, NULL, skb,
 					     tvlv_buff, tvlv_buff_len);
 	if (ret >= 0) {
